# HAWS — Human-AI Working Standard for Cursor

This repository operates under the Human-AI Working Standard (HAWS). All Cursor AI interactions, Agent Composer tasks, and inline completions must comply with these guidelines.

---

## 1. Core Operating Standards

Before proposing edits or writing code, adhere to:
- **Core Standard**: [core/HAWS.md](../../core/HAWS.md) (Empirical grounding, anti-hallucination rules, priority order)
- **Work Instructions**: [core/WORK_INSTRUCTIONS.md](../../core/WORK_INSTRUCTIONS.md) (Context loading, lean execution discipline)
- **Preferences & Anti-Patterns**: [core/USER_PREFERENCES.md](../../core/USER_PREFERENCES.md) and [core/ANTI_PATTERNS.md](../../core/ANTI_PATTERNS.md) (or `secondbrain/` if connected)

---

## 2. Project Architecture & Quality Contracts

Respect the established repository contracts:
- **Quality Gates**: [CONSTRAINTS.md](../../CONSTRAINTS.md) (Test coverage floors, linter checks, forbidden libraries)
- **Agent Boundaries**: [AGENTS.md](../../AGENTS.md) (Authorized scopes, allowed commands)
- **System Architecture**: [ARCHITECTURE.md](../../ARCHITECTURE.md) (System topology and component boundaries)
- **Handoff & Continuity**: [HANDOFF.md](../../HANDOFF.md) (Task state, unverified items, decisions)

---

## 3. Engineering Invariants

1. **Verify Before Completion**: Run automated tests and verify terminal exit codes before claiming tasks are done.
2. **Preserve Documentation & Comments**: Never strip existing comments, docstrings, or types.
3. **Strict LF Line Endings**: Maintain LF across all modified files.
4. **No Secret Leaks**: Never commit secrets or credentials.
